{
 "manufacturer": "inepro Metering",
 "manufacturer_slug": "inepro-metering",
 "model": "PRO1 single-phase energy meter (2026 PRO line)",
 "model_slug": "pro1",
 "short_model": "PRO1",
 "aliases": [
  "PRO1-Mod",
  "PRO1-Mod-Ba",
  "PRO1 1U AC 45A Mo T MID",
  "PRO1 1U AC 45A Mo T Ba MID",
  "1101",
  "1102"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
 "applies_to": "PRO1-Mod (art. 1101) and PRO1-Mod-Ba (art. 1102, with RTC tariffs) from the 2026 PRO1 user manual version 1.3; the PRO1-S has no Modbus.",
 "summary": "The PRO1 is a MID-certified single-phase 45 A DIN-rail energy meter from inepro's 2026 PRO line; the -Mod versions add an RS485 Modbus RTU port. Live values are IEEE 754 floats (high word first) in input registers from hex 5000h, energy counters sit from 6000h and settings from 4000h. This map covers the default register map: instantaneous values, THD, demand peaks, energy totals and tariff registers (as floats) and the main communication and display settings.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "The map prints hex addresses that go into the request unchanged; the manual's example frames are 01 06 4003 000A (set Modbus ID) and 01 10 5060 0002 ... (reset demand peak). So 5012h is wire address 20498. Rows typed 'input' are read with function 04; rows typed 'input /holding' are listed here as holding registers (read 03, write 06/16)."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "PRO1 energy meter - Full User Manual EN",
  "doc_number": "User manual version 1.3",
  "revision_date": "2026",
  "url": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6617f74190bf0a53bfd776e8/6aeca6163dcdf3a4b4b8ac7b_PRO1%20energy%20meter%20-%20Full%20User%20Manual%20EN.pdf",
  "pages": "Modbus spec p. 9; terminals p. 13; comm settings p. 35; default register map pp. 40-46; data-format note p. 56; writable registers pp. 57-59"
 },
 "notes": [
  "This file covers only the 'Default' register map. The manual also prints an 'Extensive' map (from 0000h, W/var units) and a 'YTL' map (scaled integers and UINT64 counters) but does not say how either is selected, so they are left out.",
  "Energy registers are typed 'UINT32/Float ABCD' (or INT32/Float) with units 'Wh/kWh'. Register 4026h selects the format: 1 = INT32 (default), 2 = FLOAT. They are listed here as FLOAT32 in kWh/kvarh/kVAh, valid only after writing 2 to 4026h. The INT32 mode is not covered because the manual never states its scale explicitly.",
  "The INT32/FLOAT pairing with Wh/kWh follows the order printed in the type and unit columns ('UINT32/Float', 'Wh/kWh'); the same manual's Extensive map also gives float energy in kWh.",
  "Total reactive energy (6024h) is printed with unit 'vah/kvah' in the map; it is listed here as kvarh, matching its name and the DS-T1/DS-T2 reactive totals (6026h/6028h).",
  "Registers marked 'Only for Ba version with RTC' (RTC tariff and some quadrant energies) read 0 on meters without the RTC; the manual says unsupported registers stay readable and return 0.",
  "Left out: serial number, meter code and CRC (BCD/HEX/ASCII with no decoding given), RTC time and tariff tables (BCD blocks), current direction (ASCII), S0 output rate (typed UINT16 length 1 in the read map but FLOAT length 2 in the write table), CT ratio, tariff mode 6048h (listed twice with different meanings), LCD password and the resettable day counter (INT32 without a stated word order).",
  "Quadrant labels on the DS-T1/DS-T2 rows are copied as printed; some pair import/export with Q2/Q3 differently from the totals rows.",
  "Baud rates per the manual: 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600 and 115200. Stop bits: 1 with even/odd parity, 2 with no parity.",
  "This 2026 PRO line uses a different template from the older PRO1-Mod/PRO2-Mod (V3.x) and PRO380-Mod maps; do not mix them."
 ],
